  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">During the reporting period, through the Capacity Building Program Between Australian Securities and Investments Commission (ASIC) and Vietnam State Securities Commission (SSC) program, ASIC made progress in developing its partnership with the SSC, as well strengthen SSC regulatory capacity and staff skills through the provision of virtual and in-person interactive webinars.
Through the Vietnam Australia Consumer Protection Partnership (VACCA), the Australian Commission and Consumer Commission (ACCC) provided targeted and practical technical assistance to the Vietnamese Ministry of Industry and Trade and Vietnam Competition Commission (VCC) to support effective consumer law reform and implementation in Vietnam.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 2 August 2024, the Australian Securities and Investment Commission (ASIC) signed its first Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with Vietnam&#x2019;s State Securities Commission to support information sharing arrangements under a formalised capacity building program. The MoU was signed by ASIC Chair Joe Longo and SSC Chairwoman Madam Vu Thi Chan Phuong. The MoU will enable the two agencies to establish formal information sharing mechanisms, enhance technical cooperation in market supervision, exchange best practices and boost investor protection efforts. In April 2024, ASIC delivered an interactive webinar on &#x2018;Good Governance and Risk Management&#x2019; in partnership with the SSC and the Australian Embassy in Hanoi. The SSC provided a special presentation on Vietnam&#x2019;s corporate governance regime. There were 54 participants (60 per cent women) in the webinar.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Mekong-Australia Partnership (MAP), the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission&#x2019;s (ACCC) Consumer Affairs Program (CAP) provided targeted and practical technical assistance to the Vietnam Competition Commission (VCC) and Ministry of Industry and Trade in support of effective competition law implementation, including providing input to Vietnam&#x2019;s new consumer protection law which came into effect 1 July 2024.  This cooperation under MAP complements and builds on the regional work delivered under the Agreement Establishing the ASEAN-Australia-New Zealand Free Trade Area (AANZFTA). 
&#x200d;
In 2024, the ACCC hosted two highly successful study visits where senior leaders in the VCC and ACCC met to discuss approaches to consumer law protection, regulation and empowerment. The staff exchanges have continued to strengthen the relationship between the VCC and ACCC and have ensured activities are targeted at VCC priorities. The VCC and ACCC agreed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) which was signed by VCC Chair Le Trieu Dung and ACCC Chair Gina Cass-Gottlieb and exchanged between Prime Ministers on 7 March 2024 on the sidelines of the 2024 ASEAN-Australia Special Summit.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
